# Report

## 1. `zimmRecentlyViewedRail`

**Files & line counts** (`/Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa/overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmRecentlyViewedRail/`):
- `index.tsx` — **167 lines**
- `zimmRecentlyViewedRail.css.ts` — **325 lines**
- (also `index.stories.tsx` 219, `index.test.tsx` 204, `zimmRecentlyViewedRail.css.test.ts` 65)

**Props type** — `index.tsx:26-60` (JSDoc omitted; each prop's doc summarised):

```ts
export type ZimmRecentlyViewedRailProps = {
  title: ReactNode;                              // component applies textStyle="heading3" itself
  cards: readonly ZimmRecentlyViewedCardProps[]; // rendered in order, hard-capped per breakpoint
  seeAllHref?: string;                           // link only renders when provided
  seeAllLabel?: string;                          // no intl/fallback owned here
};
```

Plus `index.tsx:18`:
```ts
export type ZimmRecentlyViewedCardProps = ZimmProductCardBaseProps & ZimmProductCardRecentlyViewedVariation;
```

**Layout — flex, NOT scroll-snap.** Scroll/scroll-snap was explicitly **removed** (`zimmRecentlyViewedRail.css.ts:74`: `GROUP'S SCROLL/SCROLL-SNAP CSS IS REMOVED (2026-09-10)`; `:300`: `// No overflow/scroll-snap CSS here any more`). No `overflowX` anywhere in either file.

`group` part (`zimmRecentlyViewedRail.css.ts:296-307`):
```ts
group: {
  display: 'flex',
  width: '100%',
  gap: 0,
  justifyContent: 'flex-start',
},
```

`card` part (`:309-323`) — each card gets a **percentage share of the row**, no fixed px width:
```ts
card: {
  flex: '0 0 auto',
  width: CARD_ROW_SHARE_MOBILE,
  minWidth: CARD_MIN_WIDTH_MOBILE_TABLET,
  [TABLET_UP_QUERY]: { width: CARD_ROW_SHARE_TABLET },
  [DESKTOP_UP_QUERY]: { width: CARD_ROW_SHARE_DESKTOP },
},
```

Named constants verbatim:
```ts
// :160
const CARD_MIN_WIDTH_MOBILE_TABLET = '12.5rem'; // 200px — confirmed Figma value ...
// :165-167
const CARD_ROW_SHARE_MOBILE  = `${(100 / RECENTLY_VIEWED_RAIL_VISIBLE_COUNTS.base).toFixed(4)}%`; // 2 cards -> 50%
const CARD_ROW_SHARE_TABLET  = `${(100 / RECENTLY_VIEWED_RAIL_VISIBLE_COUNTS.md).toFixed(4)}%`;   // 3 cards -> 33.3333%
const CARD_ROW_SHARE_DESKTOP = `${(100 / RECENTLY_VIEWED_RAIL_VISIBLE_COUNTS.xl).toFixed(4)}%`;   // 5 cards -> 20%
// :171-172
const HEADER_HEIGHT_MOBILE  = '3.5rem'; // 56px
const HEADER_HEIGHT_DESKTOP = '6rem';   // 96px
// :196-197
const RAIL_CONTENT_MAX_WIDTH_MOBILE = '47.9375rem'; // 767px
const RAIL_CONTENT_MAX_WIDTH_TABLET = '63.9375rem'; // 1023px
// :203
const TABLET_UP_QUERY  = `@media (min-width: ${breakpoints.md})`; // 768px
// :223
const DESKTOP_UP_QUERY = `@media (min-width: ${RECENTLY_VIEWED_RAIL_DESKTOP_BREAKPOINT})`; // 1024px
```
Backing counts, `/Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa/overrides/app/constants/index.ts:56` and `:67`:
```ts
export const RECENTLY_VIEWED_RAIL_VISIBLE_COUNTS = { base: 2, md: 3, xl: 5 } as const;
export const RECENTLY_VIEWED_RAIL_DESKTOP_BREAKPOINT = '64em'; // 1024px
```
Inter-card **gap is literally zero** (`gap: 0`); the only gaps are in the header row (`gap: 'var(--zimm-scale-2xl)'`, desktop `'var(--zimm-scale-3xl)'`, `:257` / `:263`).

**Title + link header — yes.** The docblock calls it `title-and-link` (`zimmRecentlyViewedRail.css.ts:9`, `:169`). Render body, `index.tsx:143-157`:
```tsx
<chakra.div __css={styles.header}>
  <chakra.span textStyle="heading3" flex="1 0 0" minWidth={0}>
    {title}
  </chakra.span>
  {seeAllHref && seeAllLabel && (
    <SeeAllLink to={seeAllHref} textStyle="linkLg" __css={styles.seeAllLink}>
      {seeAllLabel}
